# Holistics

> Holistics is an AI analytics platform built on a programmable semantic layer (AML) and a composable, AI-native query language (AQL). It lets data teams deliver self-service BI that is both powerful and reliable: analytics defined as code, queried through a governed metrics layer, and explored safely by everyone.

Holistics is built for data teams who want the control of code with the reach of self-service. Its core ideas are AML (define models, relationships, and reusable metrics as version-controlled code), AQL (a composable query language for governed metrics), and a flexible canvas for safe self-service exploration.

## Product
- [How Holistics Works](https://www.holistics.io/how-holistics-works/): An overview of the Holistics workflow, from connecting your data warehouse to governed self-service reporting.
- [Self-Service BI](https://www.holistics.io/self-service-bi/): Let everyone explore data and build reports on a governed single source of truth, without writing SQL.
- [AI Analytics](https://www.holistics.io/ai/): Explore data in natural language, grounded in the governed semantic layer for answers you can trust.
- [Embedded Analytics](https://www.holistics.io/embedded-analytics/): Embed governed dashboards and self-service exploration directly into your own product.

## Platform & Capabilities
- [Semantic Layer](https://www.holistics.io/semantic-layer/): Holistics' programmable semantic layer (AML) for defining data models, relationships, and reusable metrics as code.
- [Analytics Query Language (AQL)](https://www.holistics.io/aql/): A composable, AI-native query language for governed metrics and AI reasoning — an alternative to raw SQL.
- [Analytics as Code](https://www.holistics.io/as-code/): Version-controlled analytics: define dashboards, models, and metrics in code and ship them through Git.
- [Agentic BI Development](https://www.holistics.io/agentic-bi-coding/): Develop BI with coding agents, locally or in the browser.
- [Canvas Dashboard](https://www.holistics.io/product/canvas-dashboard/): A flexible drag-and-drop canvas for building dashboards, extensible with code.
- [Data Delivery](https://www.holistics.io/product/data-delivery/): Deliver reports and insights to the right audience on schedule, across email, Slack, and more.
- [dbt Integration](https://www.holistics.io/dbt-integration/): Connect your dbt transformation layer with the Holistics BI layer.
- [Reusable Analytics](https://www.holistics.io/reusability/): Build reusable, composable analytics components.
- [Dynamic Data Sources](https://www.holistics.io/dynamic-data-sources/): Dynamically select the data source by user and environment.
- [All Features](https://www.holistics.io/features/): Explore Holistics' full feature set and capabilities.

## Evaluate
- [Pricing](https://www.holistics.io/pricing/): Plans and pricing for teams of different sizes and use cases.
- [BI Tools Comparison](https://www.holistics.io/bi-tools/comparison/): A feature-by-feature comparison of leading BI platforms (Looker, Power BI, Tableau, Sisense, Domo, and Holistics).
- [BI Tools With a Semantic Layer](https://www.holistics.io/bi-tools/semantic-layer/): A fact-based comparison of BI tools with semantic layers, evaluated on metric expressiveness, governance, AI readiness, and self-service.

