## From the Blog
- [Analytics as Code](https://www.holistics.io/blog/analytics-as-code/): The case for treating analytics — models, metrics, and dashboards — as version-controlled code.
- [How Would an Ideal Semantic Layer Look Like?](https://www.holistics.io/blog/the-ideal-semantic-layer/): Holistics' thesis on what a semantic layer should be, and why most fall short.
- [Composable Metrics](https://www.holistics.io/blog/composable-metrics/): Why self-service analytics needs metrics that compose, and how AQL makes them composable.
- [Metrics Deserve Better Composition Than SQL Allows](https://www.holistics.io/blog/metrics-deserve-better-composition/): The limits of SQL for expressing reusable business metrics — the problem AQL was built to solve.
- [LLM Is Not Enough (for Self-Service Analytics)](https://www.holistics.io/blog/large-language-model-self-service-analytics/): Why a governed semantic layer, not an LLM alone, is what makes AI-driven self-service reliable.
- [What Is Agentic BI?](https://www.holistics.io/blog/what-is-agentic-bi/): A definition of agentic BI and how it reshapes self-service analytics.
- [AQL: A Better Query Language for Agentic Analytics](https://www.holistics.io/blog/agentic-query-language/): How AQL gives AI agents a composable, governed query interface instead of raw SQL.
- [Semantic Layer Tools: The Complete Guide](https://www.holistics.io/blog/semantic-layers/): A comprehensive guide to semantic layer tools and how they compare.

